  "description": "Not your average meatballs, these Iowa ham balls are a regional favorite in which ham and ground pork are bound with buttery crackers and tangy buttermilk, then shaped and baked in a sticky sweet sauce.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: ham steak → any thick-cut\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The assembled glaze and the raw shaped ham balls can be refrigerated separately for up to 3 days before continuing with step 5 to finish cooking.\nThe fully cooked ham balls can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.",
